# yocto: build dir (holds downloads + sstate-cache) and kas-cloned upstream
# repos. poky is gone since the move to wrynose — bitbake, openembedded-core
# and meta-yocto replaced it; the entry stays so stale clones are ignored too.
yocto/build/
yocto/local/
yocto/bitbake/
yocto/openembedded-core/
yocto/meta-yocto/
yocto/poky/
yocto/meta-openembedded/
yocto/meta-raspberrypi/
# safety net: a plain `kas-container build` (without yocto/kas.sh) drops these
# at the repo root — always prefer the wrapper, but never let them reach git
/build/
/bitbake/
/openembedded-core/
/meta-yocto/
/poky/
/meta-openembedded/
/meta-raspberrypi/
